{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch79QVZdbkMgBrfZacZMs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I left out the line saying every other publisher pays at least $12,000. Your facts don't back it up: you have one $12,500 fee, and your agent's range starts at $11,000. If the publisher knows the market, they'll know it isn't true, and that could weaken an otherwise strong case. The facts you have make the point better. Another publisher paid you $12,500 last year, and an agent's range of $11,000 to $13,000 means your $11,500 ask is modest.\n\nFill in the bracketed details before sending. The draft is about 190 words.\n\n<final_document>\nSubject: Fee for [Book Title]\n\nHi [Name],\n\nThank you for offering me [Book Title]. I'd love to illustrate it, and I'm glad to keep working together after six books.\n\nBefore I sign, I'd like to talk about the fee. My fee has been $9,000 per book since my first project with you four years ago, and a lot has changed since then. Two of our books have sold more than 20,000 copies each, and [Title] was chosen for the [State] reading list. Each book still takes me about four months of full-time work.\n\nI've also looked at what the market pays now. Last year another publisher paid me $12,500 for a 32-page book of the same scope. My agent tells me that $11,000 to $13,000 is standard for an illustrator with my track record.\n\nSo I'm asking for $11,500 for this book. That's at the lower end of the current range, because I value working with you and your team and want to keep doing it.\n\nI'm excited about this project. If it's easier to talk it through, I'm happy to set up a call.\n\nBest,\n[Your name]\n</final_document>"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5410,"cache_read_input_tokens":3853,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5410},"out